  F2 (accuracy of the brief's C6 phrasing, not a defect in the code).
    apply_changes calls deps.Settings.ApplyOverrides IN-PROCESS
    (register.go:236); it does not go through POST /whatif/apply. Grepping
    web/, cmd/ and all *.go for "whatif/apply" finds only the route
    registration (handlers.go:851) and the test helper -- there is no
    in-repo HTTP client of the endpoint at all (consistent with
    docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-12-app-wide-mcp-design.md:83, "retained
    without a consumer"). So the new 400 cannot break a live caller, which is
    the substance of the criterion and is satisfied; but apply_changes is a
    caller of ApplyOverrides, not of the guarded endpoint.
  F3 (residual, by design of this task's scope). ApplyOverrides itself still
    treats expectedScenario == "" as "no expectation" (settings.go:1166,
    unchanged from master). The requirement now lives only in the HTTP
    handler, so any future in-process caller that passes "" still gets an
    unguarded write. The brief explicitly scopes ApplyOverrides as untouched,
    so this is a note, not a miss.
